  "verbalization": "Telmisartan is classified as an Angiotensin 2 Receptor Antagonist, a class of drugs that exerts its therapeutic effects by blocking the action of angiotensin II, a hormone that causes vasoconstriction and increases blood pressure. This classification is shared with other members of the Angiotensin 2 Receptor Antagonists family, such as Irbesartan, Valsartan, and Losartan, all of which are known to treat hypertension. The evidence from the visible paths indicates that Telmisartan, through its inclusion in the Angiotensin 2 Receptor Antagonists class, is linked to the treatment of hypertension. The lowest common ancestors of Telmisartan and its family members—such as the Angiotensin II Receptor Antagonist category—provide a structural and ontological basis for this relationship. The consistent scores across the paths suggest a strong, well-supported connection between Telmisartan and the treatment of hypertension, reinforcing the role of angiotensin II receptor antagonists in managing this condition.",
